{"repositoryId":1160082877,"availability":"available","full":"Disha-kp/slang-life-tracker","name":"slang-life-tracker","description":"An interactive Streamlit app using NLP and live Reddit scraping to track, analyze, and score slang lifecycle trends from niche to mainstream.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Python","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-02-17T14:22:11Z","updated":"2026-10-18T10:35:53Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://slang-life-tracker.streamlit.app/","topics":["data-analytics","data-visualization","nlp","plotly","python","reddit-api","slang-tracker","streamlit"],"demo":"https://slang-life-tracker.streamlit.app/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T02:49:53.190Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-19T02:49:53.190Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-19T02:49:53.190Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-19T02:49:53.190Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["The Slang Life Tracker is an advanced linguistic analysis tool designed to track the lifecycle of slang terms from their obscure origins to mainstream saturation and eventual \"cringe\" status.","Unlike static dictionaries, this application uses a dynamic, multi-layered approach:","The project now features Deep Lore Integration, visualizing slang evolution on a 400-Year Chronos Timeline, placing modern terms like \"Rizz\" alongside 17th-century insults like \"Zounds\" to show the cyclical nature of language."],"features":["Layer 1 (The Archive): Consults a curated database of historical and modern slang (1600s - 2026).","Layer 2 (Deep Search): If a term is unknown, it scrapes live Reddit data (r/all) to discover its usage context, sentiment, and current relevance.","Lifecycle Analysis: Calculates a \"Cringe Score\" and \"Cultural Capital\" to determine if a word is Niche, Peak, Mainstream, or Dead."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Disha-kp/slang-life-tracker/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"288576169d531d